{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The outdoor heavy-duty tape felt relevant because my recent anchors and outdoor wood screws suggest mounting tasks where a light-duty adhesive option could be useful, provided it suits the surface.",
    "The other industrial-strength VELCRO also fits that mounting purpose, although I would choose only one suitable roll for the immediate task."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The connectors, heat-shrink tubing, electrical tape, and toggle switch require a wiring or repair need that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "The wire wheel, caliper, and thread gauges serve grinding or precision metalworking tasks; buying packaged framing nails and wood screws does not give me a reason to use them.",
    "The narrow hook-and-loop roll offers fastening in a broad sense, but I have no specific need for that format alongside the outdoor mounting tape."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying construction fasteners seems to have been taken as interest in almost any workshop supply, even when it serves a different task.",
    "The recommendations treated tapes and fastening products as broadly interchangeable, while their surface compatibility, strength, and intended use determine whether I need them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of framing nails, wood screws, and drywall anchors point most clearly toward fastening wood and mounting objects, rather than electrical work.",
    "The dimensions, coatings, and compatibility details in my recent fastener purchases matter because supplies need to fit the material, tool, and job.",
    "The medicine cups and vacuum bags meet separate practical needs; they do not establish a reason for me to buy unrelated workshop equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my mounting needs but stretched that interest into electrical and metalworking supplies without a clear task connection."
}"}
